 a percentage. The dblock line share is wrong.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer A credits Kochnev with 537 of the exposure lines, which is about 70% after copy detection, and notes that McCarthy and Yunin left. But it recommends Marco Silva as an active reviewer with no stand-in framing. It also never says that active people own at most 8% of the directory.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer A says Kochnev owns 71 of about 120 lines (about 59%), which is below the 68-82% range. It also doesn't say that active people own 0% of the delegator code. It does not credit Marco with the code. It names Marc Rohloff as the closest active person, but only for behavior, not as a line owner. It misses the range.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer A uses copy detection to credit grouped_exposure.rb mostly to Kochnev (100 lines) and says Marco has only 12 of those lines. It doesn't give a repo-wide percentage for Marco. It mentions Anna's inspect/error message change and does not credit it to Marco. It then recommends Marco as the reviewer, but the criterion's credit points are satisfied.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer A says Lena's lines are mostly copyright headers and so not ownership, which is acceptable. It never gives a departed-share figure of 79-90%. It also doesn't give Subbota's and Scholz's line shares, though it does call Scholz departed and Subbota active. The missing departed-share figure fails the criterion.\", \"pass\": false}], \"B\": [{\"n\": 1, \"reason\": \"Answer B puts dblock's commit share at 18.2% (52 commits), below the 20% floor, so the identities are not fully merged. It puts Kochnev at 18.7% of lines, below 21%, and dblock at 10.4% of lines and described as inactive since 2016. Both figures are wrong.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer B gives Kochnev only 54%, and credits Marco Silva with 19% of the directory as an active reviewer. That is the failure mode the criterion describes: an active person credited with a large share of the exposure code.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer B gives Kochnev 71% non-blank lines, within the range. It also says the delegators/ lines were moved and credit stays with the original authors. But it says Marco has 4 lines (4%), and it presents Marco as a reviewer by default. It doesn't say active people own 0% of the whole delegator code, since it lists Marco at 4%. Marco isn't credited with 10% or more, and no active owner is named. The overall result is borderline, but the answer says nobody who wrote delegator code is active.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer B credits Marco with 117 lines of the exposure code, and says Marco wrote 100% of grouped_exposure.rb. That fails the criterion, which requires credit going to Kochnev. Marco's 3%-or-more repo share is also implied.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer B says people with no commit in the last year own 89.3% of non-blank lines, which is within the 79-90% range. It says dependabot's lines are excluded and Lena's commit was set aside as boilerplate. It does not name Scholz's line share as about 4% (it says 7.9%), and it doesn't say Subbota is active. The overall shape passes, though the individual figures are imprecise.\", \"pass\": true}], \"C\": [{\"n\": 1, \"reason\": \"Answer C merges dblock's names and gives 119 commits, which is correct. It names Kochnev as the top line owner, with 756 lib/ lines and 1,190 with spec, and says dblock has about 242 surviving lines. That is close to the truth of 286. It says Kochnev left in 2015. It gives no percentages, but the rank and numbers are broadly right.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer C gives Kochnev 496 lines (69%), and notes McCarthy and Yunin are inactive. It explains that Marco's lines are copied and don't count, and it says no active person has real depth. It recommends Andrei Subbota and dblock as routing stand-ins. It does not give the 2.6% figure. It does say nobody active owns the code. It lists Lena at 20 lines, but flags them as headers.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer C uses git log --follow to trace the delegators back to the original authors, with Kochnev at about 71 lines. It says everyone in that history has been inactive for 3+ years. It does not credit Marco with the code, and names no active owner. Kochnev's share isn't given as a percentage, but the line count matches the truth's range.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer C says Marco's 143 plain-blame lines in grouped_exposure.rb go back to Kochnev and others under copy detection. It doesn't credit Marco with significant code, and credits Anna's 5-line change to Anna rather than Marco. That meets the criterion.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer C says Lena's 20 lines are copyright headers, so they are flagged and don't count as ownership. It says Scholz is gone and Subbota is active. But it gives no departed-share figure of 79-90%, and it lists Lena with 20 lines in its exposure table. The missing departed share fails the criterion.\", \"pass\": false}]}","ttft_ms":15906,"type":"result","duration_ms":15933,"uuid":"5135eae2-7a6d-49f5-ab3b-503139388e46","ttft_stream_ms":2995,"time_to_request_ms":452,"first_content_frame_ms":2995,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
